Subject: vmwarefusion: allow CPU hot-add

docker-machine-ctl resize grows the running VM through VMware's hot-add. Upstream's template already
allows memory hot-add (mem.hotadd); CPUs need vcpu.hotadd too. Payload's prepare_vmx makes the same
change to a VM created before this (2026-11-24).

--- a/drivers/vmwarefusion/vmx_darwin.go
+++ b/drivers/vmwarefusion/vmx_darwin.go
@@ -51,8 +51,9 @@
 sata0:2.deviceType = "cdrom-image"
 {{ end }}
 vmci0.present = "TRUE"
 mem.hotadd = "TRUE"
+vcpu.hotadd = "TRUE"
 memsize = "{{.Memory}}"
 powerType.powerOff = "soft"
 powerType.powerOn = "soft"
 powerType.reset = "soft"
